I really have no idea if this would work or not (or if it's been done
before), but I'm throwing it out as an idea anyway.

The other day I was thinking about voluntary conducts. What about a
pragmatist conduct? The definition of a pragmatist would be a person
who does not believe in magic, in any way, shape, or form. As an
illustration, imagine the most hard-headed of scientists going through
the dungeon, thoroughly convinced that everything he/she experiences
can be explained by the laws of nature. :-)

Spellbooks would obviously be off limits. So would scrolls, rings or
amulets, because what scientist would believe that you could produce
an effect in the real world simply by pronouncing a few arcane words,
or wearing a piece of jewelery? Some wands would be permissible, I
think, because wands of fire, cold, digging, magic missile and so
forth are really just glorified laser guns. On the other hand, sleep,
polymorph, teleportation and *definitely* wishing would be out of
bounds. Same goes for potions: I could see a pragmatist drinking a
potion of healing, gain strength, hallucination and so forth, but
certainly not polymorph or levitation. A pragmatist would not carry
around luckstones or consciously try to increase his/her luck. Rubbing
lamps would be a no-no.

I can foresee a few problems with this. The first would be identifying
objects. If no scrolls are allowed, there goes your only sure method
of identifying things. And then how would the pragmatist avoid
drinking forbidden potions or using forbidden wands? I think that
*one* use of a forbidden potion or wand would be forgivable, because a
scientist could explain the experience away by saying it was some
weird dream or hallucination. But if the player actively seeks out
that type of potion/wand to use it again, he or she obviously believes
in magic and is therefore not a pragmatist.

The second problem would, of course, be magic resistance. After all,
if you don't believe in magic, you won't try to defend yourself
against possible magic attacks. And yet (as I just discovered to my
rue) it is very difficult, if not impossible, to get past the higher
levels without magic resistance, particularly to avoid touch of death
and the like. I think the pragmatist could wear gray dragon scale mail
-- after all, it has many advantages other than magic resistance (its
lightness, good protection etc.) Magicbane is a little less
permissible, unless the player's main skill class is dagger (i.e.
Ranger) and they're carrying it around just because it's a good
weapon.

So what do you think? Would it be possible?

